---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="About" description="What Zero to HYPE is, who writes it, and how its facts are checked.">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>About Zero to HYPE</h1>
    <p>
      Zero to HYPE is a free roadmap for developers building on Hyperliquid. Each topic links the
      official documentation and the best tutorials others have written, then adds what those
      leave out: worked formulas, labs you can run in the browser, and notes from running real
      services against the API.
    </p>
    <h2>How facts are checked</h2>
    <p>
      Hyperliquid changes its API often and documents some of it late. Every lesson says when it
      was last checked against the live API, and the <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a> records
      what changed in the API each day.
    </p>
    <h2>Who writes it</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/vignesh-chaturvedi">Vignesh Chaturvedi</a>, a contributor to <a
        href="https://github.com/infinitefield/hypersdk">hypersdk</a> and the author of <a
        href="https://github.com/vignesh-chaturvedi/hyperkeeper">hyperkeeper</a>, an open-source
      operations tool for HIP-3 and HIP-4 deployers.
    </p>
    <h2>Independent</h2>
    <p>
      Zero to HYPE is not affiliated with or endorsed by Hyperliquid. Labs only ever use testnet
      and keys generated in your browser; never paste a real private key into any site,
      including this one.
    </p>
    <h2>Licences</h2>
    <p>Code is MIT-licensed. Lessons and other content are CC BY 4.0: reuse them with credit.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
